Subject: Connector/C: report the real connect error, not EINPROGRESS

pvio_socket_internal_connect() connects a non-blocking socket: connect()
fails with EINPROGRESS, poll() waits, and getsockopt(SO_ERROR) gives the
real result, which is returned. pvio_socket_connect() builds its message
from socket_errno (errno), which still holds connect()'s EINPROGRESS. So a
connection that timed out or was refused without --connect-timeout
reported "Can't connect to server on ... (36)" on OpenVMS (115 on Linux).
With --connect-timeout the poll() timeout set errno to ETIMEDOUT, so 60
was shown. Set errno to the SO_ERROR value before returning it.

--- a/libmariadb/plugins/pvio/pvio_socket.c	2026-10-09 14:48:52.673166541 +0100
+++ b/libmariadb/plugins/pvio/pvio_socket.c	2026-10-09 14:48:52.674738261 +0100
@@ -547,7 +547,12 @@
                            (char *)&error, &error_len)) < 0)
         return errno;
       else if (error) 
+      {
+        /* The caller reports socket_errno, which still holds connect()'s
+           EINPROGRESS: report the connection's real error instead. */
+        errno= error;
         return error;
+      }
     }
   }
 #ifdef __APPLE__
